{
  "id": "COMPOUND:21580 - PROTEIN:4911",
  "verbalization": "Tomentosanol D appears to interact with CD276 antigen through a shared target of 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which is identified as a common intermediate in multiple pathways. This suggests that Tomentosanol D may act as a modulator of the downstream signaling cascade initiated by this compound. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Tomentosanol D targets different molecules—MOVP-3, SQ20B, and SNB-78—each of which is ultimately targeted by 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which in turn targets CD276 antigen. This implies that Tomentosanol D may influence the expression or activity of CD276 antigen through a series of intermediate targets, potentially modulating the immune response or other biological processes involving CD276. The consistent involvement of 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One as a central mediator across the pathways strengthens the hypothesis that Tomentosanol D exerts its effects via this molecular bridge.",
